From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 13:10:14 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/27] Slot eviction (VICTORY_SLOT_EVICT=1, off): table reads
 count as use, two lines

A texture a draw reads through a table every frame never asks for its
host copy again (`HostHeap::mirror` finds the slot showing it already),
so its last use stayed old although it was on screen: the eviction took
it as idle and the next draw made it again. Now a texture any of whose
slots a draw's table showed after "idle time ago" is kept. That frame is
read from a ring of (frame, time) points the sweep keeps, once a second;
each slot's table stamp says the frame it was last shown (`seen_since`,
31-bit, erring toward "used"). Nothing is added to the draw path.

Eviction now starts above VICTORY_SLOT_EVICT_PERCENT (85) and goes on
until the card is under VICTORY_SLOT_EVICT_LOW_PERCENT (high - 10), at
most VICTORY_SLOT_EVICT_MB (256) a sweep (`slot_plan`), instead of
freeing the excess over one line every second. As before: only textures
whose every slot a table showed lately (which its draw makes again), and
none a list holds; slots nulled first, the copy retired behind running
submissions, by the sweep, which runs with nothing in the air; a texture
that came back is not taken again for 60 s.

The memory CSV gets the eviction's counts (evicted, MB, slots reset, came
back, within 2 s, given up) and its state (evicting, candidates, kept as
seen by a table, blocked by slots picked by index).

(cherry picked from commit 6497c6e37e8377b60054ff507fb430a1ac1863a9)
